        "title": "GymVisual #627212, Dumbbell Larsen Press (male), video (movement reference)",
        "url": "https://gymvisual.com/videos/15749-dumbbell-larsen-press-male.html"
      },
      {
        "id": "muyor2019",
        "title": "Muyor, Rodríguez-Ridao, Martín-Fuentes and Antequera-Vique 2019, evaluation and comparison of electromyographic activity in bench press with feet on the ground and active hip flexion (PLoS ONE 14(6):e0218209; PMC6568408)",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6568408/"
      },
      {
        "id": "saeterbakken2011",
        "title": "Saeterbakken, van den Tillaar and Fimland 2011, a comparison of muscle activity and 1-RM strength of three chest-press exercises with different stability requirements (J Sports Sci 29(5):533-538; PubMed 21225489)",
        "url": "https://read.qxmd.com/read/21225489/a-comparison-of-muscle-activity-and-1-rm-strength-of-three-chest-press-exercises-with-different-stability-requirements"
      }
    ],
    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Get into position safely: sit on the end of the bench with the dumbbells on the thighs, then lie back and kick them up one knee at a time; at the end of the set bring them back to the thighs or lower them to the floor beside the bench rather than dropping them (clinical opinion). Put the feet on the floor to get up and down; lift the legs only once the dumbbells are up.",
        "Holding the legs up loads the hip flexors and the low back; Muyor 2019 suggests caution for this reason. Skip it with low back pain (clinical opinion).",
        "Keep the wrists straight over the forearms; bent-back wrists under a heavy dumbbell strain the wrist.",
        "Stop if sharp pain, numbness or tingling occurs.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "Bend the knees and keep the feet hovering (hips and knees at 90 degrees) if the straight legs pull on the low back.",
        "Rest the heels lightly on the floor while learning."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Dumbbell bench press with the feet planted.",
        "Dumbbell floor press."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Heavier dumbbells.",
        "Longer pause at the bottom.",
        "Single-arm Larsen press."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "pec_r": "Main pusher. With the feet off the floor (hips flexed, knees at 90 degrees) every recorded muscle was more active than with the feet planted, the pectoralis remaining the most active (Muyor 2019, barbell at 60% 1RM).",
      "pec_l": "Main pusher. With the feet off the floor (hips flexed, knees at 90 degrees) every recorded muscle was more active than with the feet planted, the pectoralis remaining the most active (Muyor 2019, barbell at 60% 1RM).",
      "ant_deltoid_r": "Flexes the shoulder with the chest.",
      "ant_deltoid_l": "Flexes the shoulder with the chest.",
      "triceps_r": "Straightens the elbows in the top half of the press.",
      "triceps_l": "Straightens the elbows in the top half of the press.",
      "serratus_r": "Holds the shoulder blades against the rib cage while each arm moves on its own.",
      "serratus_l": "Holds the shoulder blades against the rib cage while each arm moves on its own.",
      "biceps_r": "Works as a stabiliser: biceps activity rose with the stability demand, highest with dumbbells (Saeterbakken 2011).",
      "biceps_l": "Works as a stabiliser: biceps activity rose with the stability demand, highest with dumbbells (Saeterbakken 2011).",
      "forearm_flexors_r": "Grip the dumbbell handles.",
      "forearm_flexors_l": "Grip the dumbbell handles.",
      "infraspinatus_r": "Rotator cuff: centres the head of the upper arm while the dumbbells balance freely (clinical opinion).",
      "infraspinatus_l": "Rotator cuff: centres the head of the upper arm while the dumbbells balance freely (clinical opinion).",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_r": "Keep the shoulder blades drawn back and down on the bench.",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_l": "Keep the shoulder blades drawn back and down on the bench.",
      "core": "No leg drive and no foot support: the trunk must hold the body steady on the bench. Rectus abdominis activity more than doubled with the feet suspended in Muyor 2019.",
      "obliques_r": "External oblique activity rose about fourfold with the feet suspended (Muyor 2019) to keep the body from rolling.",
      "obliques_l": "External oblique activity rose about fourfold with the feet suspended (Muyor 2019) to keep the body from rolling.",
      "quads_r": "Hold the legs straight and off the floor (rectus femoris activity rose sharply with the feet suspended in Muyor 2019, there with the hips flexed).",
      "quads_l": "Hold the legs straight and off the floor (rectus femoris activity rose sharply with the feet suspended in Muyor 2019, there with the hips flexed)."
    }
  },
